{
 "title": "Why is Chernobyl abandoned?",
 "narration": "Why is Chernobyl abandoned? In April nineteen eighty-six, a safety test went wrong, and reactor four exploded in Soviet Ukraine. Three kilometres away stood Pripyat, a city of nearly fifty thousand people. For thirty-six hours, life went on as normal. Then the whole city was emptied in one afternoon. The radiation drifted north. Belarus was hit hardest, and alarms in Sweden revealed the secret to the world. The zone grew to thirty kilometres, and more than one hundred thousand people left. Today, forests and wild animals are taking the towns back.",
